  "label": "Budget Allocator",
  "group": "Worked examples",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "note",
      "type": "NoteNode",
      "x": 249,
      "y": 1154,
      "init": {
        "label": "Budget Allocator",
        "body": "# Spend by what you value\nEach thing you're buying has a price **range** (a floor and a ceiling) and a **weight** for how much you value it. **Fit budget** spends the whole budget in proportion to the weights, kept inside every range; when a category hits its ceiling the slack flows to the rest.\n\nHere: 100,000 over five categories, Housing valued 3x. The allocator returns each **Allocation** and its **Share** of the spend. The grouped steps join the price range back in and work out the **Headroom** left under each ceiling.\n\nTwo more modes on the card: **Min for target** and **Min proportional**. No solver, just arithmetic.",
        "color": "teal",
        "width": 420,
        "height": 160
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "items",
      "type": "FrameInputNode",
      "x": -100,
      "y": 625,
      "init": {
        "label": "Budget items",
        "frameText": "[{\"name\":\"Category\",\"type\":\"string\",\"values\":[\"Car\",\"Housing\",\"Furniture\",\"Tech\",\"Travel\"]},{\"name\":\"Min\",\"type\":\"number\",\"values\":[20000,15000,3000,2000,1000]},{\"name\":\"Max\",\"type\":\"number\",\"values\":[50000,60000,15000,12000,10000]},{\"name\":\"Weight\",\"type\":\"number\",\"values\":[2,3,1,1,1]}]"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "alloc",
      "type": "AllocatorNode",
      "x": 338,
      "y": 830,
      "init": {
        "label": "Allocator",
        "mode": "budget"
      },
      "literals": {
        "amount": 100000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "grp-enrich",
      "type": "GroupNode",
